{
  "_comment": "Ride height requirements are not in OpenStreetMap. This file is re-applied on every rebuild of the venue, keyed by POI name. Compiled from published 2026 Cedar Point height charts, reconciled across three of them: the absolute floor is `min`, the height a rider needs to go without a grown-up is `alone`, and `max` is a genuine rider maximum. Where the charts disagreed the lower floor was taken, so the filter errs towards letting a child queue rather than ruling them out.",
  "areas": [
    "Cedar Point Shores",
    "Lighthouse Point"
  ],
  "_areas_comment": "Named areas this venue owns that its own OpenStreetMap polygon does not cover. Cedar Point is mapped as three rings on one peninsula — the amusement park, the water park and the campground — and without this the build reads the latter two as the retail park over the road and drops everything standing in them.",
  "credits": "Height requirements were compiled from published 2026 Cedar Point height charts.",
